  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6640d0b7014bcf743ac082c8476883b3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UI_SpeechBubbleManager
  messageText: {fileID: 222246471}
  talkingAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
  interactionVisual: {fileID: 537111619}
  speechBubbleContainer: {fileID: 208172901}
  playerTransform: {fileID: 1876935962}
  activationRadius: 5
  exitRadiusCooldown: 2
  cooldownTime: 3
  typingSpeed: 0.02
  messageArray:
  - Have you tried using the Power of the <color=#00E2FB>Rabbit Soul</color> while
    <color=#00E2FB>jumping</color> up a <color=#00E2FB>Wall</color>?
  - You did figure how out you can <color=#00E2FB>jump up</color> the <color=#00E2FB>Walls</color>,
    right?
  - Well, most of them. You can <color=#00E2FB>see</color> which ones will be <color=#00E2FB>too
    slick</color> or unstable to hold on to.
  - You probably won't get up those ones.
  - But the others should be fun to jump up on!
  - <color=yellow>You can </color><color=red>WALL JUMP</color><color=yellow> on most
    Walls.</color>
  - '<color=yellow>Press </color><color=red>SPACE</color><color=yellow> when touching
    a Wall to jump off.</color> '
  - '<color=yellow>Press </color><color=red>SPACE</color><color=yellow> a </color>
    <color=red>SECOND TIME</color><color=yellow> to perform a </color> <color=red>DOUBLE
    JUMP </color> <color=yellow> while in </color><br><color=red>MID AIR</color>
    <color=yellow>.</color> '
